<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The WinRT spike.

  Not the future app - a throwaway harness for the two questions that decide
  whether LumigramPlus is worth building:

    1. Does Lumigram.Core run unchanged under the WinRT app model? It has no
       platform dependencies at all, so it should, but "should" is what this
       project exists to replace.

    2. Does ControlChannelTrigger actually wake a Windows Phone 8.1 app when data
       arrives on its socket? That is the replacement for the geolocation trick,
       which has no equivalent here - JabberWP moved off WinRT for exactly this
       reason.

  Core is linked rather than referenced, and its own AssemblyInfo excluded, so the
  same sources are compiled by the phone app, the desktop harness and this.
-->
